# Your own .pub files. The five samples already committed here stay
# tracked -- a gitignore rule does not untrack what is already in, and CI
# converts them as its isolation test. Anything added from now on is
# private to your working copy, which also means `git clean -fdx` will
# delete it.
files/

# Isolated workspaces and the scratch a plan's execution keeps beside it.
# Both are working state, not source: the worktree is a second checkout of
# this same repo, and .superpowers holds a run's ledger and review
# packages, which the git history supersedes once the work lands.
.claude/worktrees/
.superpowers/
